<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">implūmis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inpl-</span></b> ), e, adj.
		2. in-pluma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without feathers</i>, <i>unfledged</i>, <i>callow.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assidens implumibus pullis avis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 1, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fetus columbarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 64, § 170</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coni (galearum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 421</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6, 716</span></i>. — *
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>without hair</i>,
				<i>bald</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliud in utero pilis vestitum, aliud inplume,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 55, 81, § 219</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
